# UGUI with TEngine UIModule

## Overview

This project uses **UGUI** (Unity UI) with **TEngine UIModule** for UI management. All UI classes inherit from `UIWindow` or `UIWidget` and are managed by the `UIModule`.

## Project Structure

```
Assets/
├── AssetRaw/
│   └── UI/                    # UI Prefabs
│       ├── LoginUI.prefab
│       └── BattleMainUI.prefab
└── GameScripts/
    └── HotFix/
        └── GameLogic/
            └── UI/            # UI Scripts
                ├── LoginUI/
                │   └── LoginUI.cs
                └── BattleMainUI/
                    └── BattleMainUI.cs
```

## UI Base Classes

### UIWindow (Fullscreen/Popup Windows)

```csharp
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI;
using TEngine;
using GameLogic;

namespace GameLogic
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Login UI window.
    /// </summary>
    [Window(UILayer.UI, location: "LoginUI")]
    public class LoginUI : UIWindow
    {
        #region Auto-generated UI Bindings
        private Button _btnLogin;
        private InputField _inputUsername;
        private Text _txtStatus;
        
        protected override void ScriptGenerator()
        {
            _btnLogin = FindChildComponent<Button>("m_btnLogin");
            _inputUsername = FindChildComponent<InputField>("m_inputUsername");
            _txtStatus = FindChildComponent<Text>("m_txtStatus");
        }
        #endregion

        protected override void OnCreate()
        {
            // UI initialization - called once when UI is created
            base.OnCreate();
        }

        protected override void OnShow()
        {
            // Called when UI is shown
            base.OnShow();
            BindEvents();
        }

        protected override void OnRefresh()
        {
            // Called when UI is shown or refreshed
            // Use this to reset UI state (e.g., reset score, hide panels)
            base.OnRefresh();
            m_textScore.text = "Score : 0";
            m_goOverView.SetActive(false);
        }

        protected override void RegisterEvent()
        {
            // Register UI events - called automatically after OnShow
            // Use AddUIEvent to listen to game events
            AddUIEvent<int>(ActorEventDefine.ScoreChange, OnScoreChange);
            AddUIEvent(ActorEventDefine.GameOver, OnGameOver);
        }

        protected override void OnUpdate()
        {
            // Called every frame while UI is visible
            base.OnUpdate();
        }

        protected override void OnHide()
        {
            // Called when UI is hidden
            base.OnHide();
            UnbindEvents();
        }

        protected override void OnDestroy()
        {
            // Called when UI is destroyed
            base.OnDestroy();
        }

        private void BindEvents()
        {
            if (_btnLogin != null)
            {
                _btnLogin.onClick.AddListener(OnLoginClicked);
            }
        }

        private void UnbindEvents()
        {
            if (_btnLogin != null)
            {
                _btnLogin.onClick.RemoveListener(OnLoginClicked);
            }
        }

        private void OnLoginClicked()
        {
            string username = _inputUsername?.text ?? "";
            // Handle login logic
            GameModule.UI.CloseUI<LoginUI>();
        }
    }
}
```

### UIWidget (Reusable Components)

```csharp
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI;
using GameLogic;

namespace GameLogic
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Health bar widget.
    /// </summary>
    public class HealthBarWidget : UIWidget
    {
        private Slider _sliderHealth;
        private Text _txtHealth;

        protected override void ScriptGenerator()
        {
            _sliderHealth = FindChildComponent<Slider>("m_sliderHealth");
            _txtHealth = FindChildComponent<Text>("m_txtHealth");
        }

        public void SetHealth(float current, float max)
        {
            if (_sliderHealth != null)
            {
                _sliderHealth.value = current / max;
            }
            
            if (_txtHealth != null)
            {
                _txtHealth.text = $"{current:F0}/{max:F0}";
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Window Attribute

Use `[Window]` attribute to configure UI window:

```csharp
[Window(
    UILayer.UI,                    // Window layer (Bottom, UI, Top, Tips, System)
    location: "LoginUI",           // Asset name (optional, defaults to class name)
    fullScreen: false,              // Fullscreen window (optional)
    hideTimeToClose: 10             // Auto-close after hide time in seconds (optional)
)]
public class LoginUI : UIWindow { }
```

### UI Layers

```csharp
public enum UILayer : int
{
    Bottom = 0,    // Background UI
    UI = 1,         // Normal UI
    Top = 2,        // Top layer UI
    Tips = 3,       // Tips/Notifications
    System = 4,    // System UI
}
```

## UI Management

### Showing UI

```csharp
// Show UI asynchronously (preferred)
GameModule.UI.ShowUIAsync<LoginUI>();

// Show UI with user data
GameModule.UI.ShowUIAsync<LoginUI>(userData1, userData2);

// Show UI synchronously (use sparingly)
GameModule.UI.ShowUI<LoginUI>();

// Show UI and wait for it to load
var loginUI = await GameModule.UI.ShowUIAwait<LoginUI>();
```

### Closing/Hiding UI

```csharp
// Close UI (destroys the UI)
GameModule.UI.CloseUI<LoginUI>();

// Hide UI (keeps UI in memory)
GameModule.UI.HideUI<LoginUI>();
```

### Accessing UI Instance

```csharp
// Get UI instance if it exists
var loginUI = GameModule.UI.GetWindow<LoginUI>();
if (loginUI != null)
{
    // UI is already open
}
```

## UI Component Binding

### Auto-Generated Bindings

The framework provides auto-generated UI component bindings via `ScriptGenerator()` method:

```csharp
protected override void ScriptGenerator()
{
    // Find components by path
    _btnLogin = FindChildComponent<Button>("m_btnLogin");
    _inputField = FindChildComponent<InputField>("m_inputUsername");
    
    // Find GameObjects
    _panelMain = FindChild("m_panelMain").gameObject;
    
    // Find by type (if unique)
    _canvas = GetComponent<Canvas>();
}
```

### Helper Methods

```csharp
// Find child component by path
T FindChildComponent<T>(string path) where T : Component;

// Find child GameObject by path
Transform FindChild(string path);

// Get component on this GameObject
T GetComponent<T>();

// Get component in children
T GetComponentInChildren<T>();

// Get component in parent
T GetComponentInParent<T>();
```

## UI Lifecycle

```
OnCreate()     → Called once when UI is created
    ↓
OnShow()       → Called when UI is shown
    ↓
RegisterEvent() → Called after OnShow to register event listeners
    ↓
OnRefresh()    → Called after RegisterEvent to reset UI state
    ↓
OnUpdate()     → Called every frame while visible
    ↓
OnHide()       → Called when UI is hidden
    ↓
OnDestroy()    → Called when UI is destroyed
```

### Event Registration

```csharp
protected override void RegisterEvent()
{
    // Register event listeners using AddUIEvent
    // Events are automatically unregistered when UI is hidden/destroyed
    
    // Event with no parameters
    AddUIEvent(ActorEventDefine.GameOver, OnGameOver);
    
    // Event with one parameter
    AddUIEvent<int>(ActorEventDefine.ScoreChange, OnScoreChange);
    
    // Event with multiple parameters
    AddUIEvent<Vector3, Quaternion>(ActorEventDefine.PlayerDead, OnPlayerDead);
}

private void OnScoreChange(int score)
{
    m_textScore.text = $"Score : {score}";
}

private void OnGameOver()
{
    m_goOverView.SetActive(true);
}
```

## Event System Integration

### Using Event Interfaces

```csharp
// Define event interface
public interface ILoginUI : IEvent
{
    void ShowLoginUI();
}

// Implement in UI class
public class LoginUI : UIWindow, ILoginUI
{
    public void ShowLoginUI()
    {
        GameModule.UI.ShowUIAsync<LoginUI>();
    }
}

// Access from anywhere
GameEvent.Get<ILoginUI>().ShowLoginUI();
```

## Best Practices

### ✅ DO

- Inherit from `UIWindow` or `UIWidget`
- Use `[Window]` attribute for configuration
- Place UI scripts in `HotFix/GameLogic/UI/`
- Place UI prefabs in `AssetRaw/UI/`
- Use `ScriptGenerator()` for component bindings
- Use `RegisterEvent()` to register event listeners
- Use `OnRefresh()` to reset UI state when shown
- Use `AddUIEvent` in `RegisterEvent()` for event handling
- Unbind events in `OnHide()` or `OnDestroy()` (automatic for AddUIEvent)
- Use `GameModule.UI` for UI management
- Use async methods (`ShowUIAsync`) when possible

### ❌ DON'T

- Don't use `GameObject.Find()` or `Transform.Find()` in Update
- Don't create UI manually with `Instantiate()` - use `GameModule.UI`
- Don't access UI components without null checks
- Don't forget to unbind events
- Don't put UI code in main domain (use hot update domain)
- Don't use `Resources.Load()` for UI prefabs (use YooAsset via framework)

## Performance Tips

- UI components are cached in `ScriptGenerator()` - don't query repeatedly
- Use `OnUpdate()` sparingly - only when needed
- Hide UI instead of closing if it will be shown again soon
- Use object pooling for frequently created/destroyed UI elements
- Batch UI updates when possible
